{"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/writeDOT(to:)"},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Systems"}],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"writeDOT","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"to","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"inout","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TextOutputStream","preciseIdentifier":"s:s16TextOutputStreamP","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"extendedModule":"Systems","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/ECS\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Systems\/Profiling.swift#L146","fileName":"Profiling.swift"},"roleHeading":"Instance Method","role":"symbol","title":"writeDOT(to:)","externalID":"s:7Systems8ScheduleV8writeDOT2toyxz_ts16TextOutputStreamRzlF","symbolKind":"method"},"abstract":[{"text":"Writes the schedule’s dependency graph in the DOT language, for drawing with Graphviz.","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"writeDOT","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"to","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"output","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"inout","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TextOutputStream","preciseIdentifier":"s:s16TextOutputStreamP","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"parameters":[{"name":"output","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The stream to write the DOT text to."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"parameters"},{"mentions":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SchedulingSystems"],"kind":"mentions"},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","level":2,"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use this method to see why systems run in the order they do, and which could run at the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same time. Each system is a node labeled with its type’s name, numbered in the order the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"schedule runs them. An arc from one system to another means the second runs after the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"first: solid when an ordering constraint orders them, dashed when only their accesses"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"conflict. Arcs that other arcs imply are left out."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let frame = Schedule {","    Gravity()","    Movement().after(Gravity.self)","    Scoring()","}","var dot = \"\"","frame.writeDOT(to: &dot)","","let lines = dot.split(separator: \"\\n\").map { line in line.drop { $0 == \"\\t\" } }","print(lines)","\/\/ Prints \"[\"digraph {\", \"0 [label=Gravity];\", \"1 [label=Movement];\", \"2 [label=Scoring];\", \"0 -> 1;\", \"1 -> 2 [style=dashed];\", \"}\"]\""],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Laid out, the DOT text shows that ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Movement"},{"text":" is ordered after ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Gravity"},{"text":", and that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Scoring"},{"text":" runs after ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Movement"},{"text":" only because it reads the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Position"},{"text":" that ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Movement"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"writes:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"dot","code":["digraph {","    0 [label=Gravity];","    1 [label=Movement];","    2 [label=Scoring];","    0 -> 1;","    1 -> 2 [style=dashed];","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O("},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"s"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":"²) for "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"s","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" systems."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note","name":"Complexity","type":"aside"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/systems\/schedule\/writedot(to:)"]}],"sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Inspecting-a-Schedule","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/systems","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/names","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/ambiguities()","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Ambiguity"],"title":"Inspecting a Schedule"}],"references":{"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems":{"kind":"symbol","role":"collection","title":"Systems","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems","url":"\/documentation\/systems","abstract":[{"text":"Declare the rules of a simulation as systems, and run them on a world in a schedule.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule/ambiguities()":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/ambiguities()","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule\/ambiguities()","role":"symbol","title":"ambiguities()","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ambiguities","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7Systems9AmbiguityV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Ambiguity"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Returns every pair of systems whose accesses conflict but that no ordering constraint"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"orders."}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/SchedulingSystems":{"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedulingsystems","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Order the systems of a schedule, run them only when a condition holds, and find out how a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"schedule runs them."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SchedulingSystems","kind":"article","type":"topic","title":"Scheduling Systems"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule":{"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Schedule","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule","title":"Schedule","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","abstract":[{"text":"A list of systems that run on a world, in order, and at the same time where they can.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Schedule","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule/writeDOT(to:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/writeDOT(to:)","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule\/writedot(to:)","role":"symbol","title":"writeDOT(to:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"writeDOT","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"to","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"inout","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TextOutputStream","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s16TextOutputStreamP"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Writes the schedule’s dependency graph in the DOT language, for drawing with Graphviz.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule/names":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"var","